---
/*
  Replaces /story and /team. Governance instead of a founding story.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/company".
  No team size anywhere on this page until decision 5 is made: four different
  numbers in four places are worse than no number.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import { legal } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Company | Wunder"
  description="The legal entity behind Wunder: KG Models SIA, registered in Riga, with two managing directors on the register."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>The company behind the name.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Wunder is a brand by {legal.company}, registration number {legal.regNumber}, registered on {
          legal.registered
        } at {legal.street}, {legal.city}, {legal.country}.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can look that up in the Latvian register without asking us for anything. There is a
        company with a similar name in the United States that we have nothing to do with. The
        registration number above is how you tell them apart.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Who decides.</h2>
      <p>
        Two managing directors, each with sole signing authority, both on the register: Manuel
        Gonzalez, CEO and co owner, and Lauris Kalnins, COO and co owner.
      </p>
      <p>
        Contracts are signed by {legal.company}. There is no second entity in the chain, no
        intermediary and no third party that your agreement is quietly assigned to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Where the work happens.</h2>
      <p>
        Riga is the registered seat and the office. The content and chat team works in the PHT time
        zone, which is what makes the chat cover the hours your fans are awake in.
      </p>
      <p class="caption">
        We do not publish a team size until we can define it the same way twice, split into
        employees and contractors. A number we cannot repeat is worse than no number.
      </p>
      <div class="shots">
        <Placeholder label="Office in Riga" ratio="square" />
        <Placeholder label="Production" ratio="square" />
      </div>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .shots {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 32px 0;
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .shots {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
